      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:131:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Lord, my heart is not haughty, nor mine eyes lofty: neither do I exercise myself in great matters, or in things too high for me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 131:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:131:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:131:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Surely I have behaved and quieted myself, as a child that is weaned of his mother: my soul is even as a weaned child.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 131:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:131:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:131:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Let Israel hope in the LORD from henceforth and for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 131:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:131:3"
      }
    }
